        "heading_HVeeF6": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "sub_heading": "",
            "heading": "How to Choose an Optimal Tamper-Evident Label Supplier",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h1",
            "rich_text_cstm": "<p>To win over a wide customer base, your choice of tamper-evident labels can be one of the most important decisions you make. When selecting the optimal tamper-evident label supplier, you should consider the following factors.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_69TVex": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Visual Appeal",
            "content": "<p>To stand out from your competitors, your product should be visually appealing. Tamper-evident label designs should utilize a good balance of bright and dark colors while conveying all necessary branding information and imagery. Colors should be clear and crisp, with no smears or blurring.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": true,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_jGLcdP": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Experience",
            "content": "<p>The best label supplier should have detailed, extensive knowledge of design, layout, and material choice. They should be able to settle on these factors based on where the label will be placed, whether it’s on cardboard or glass, or in extreme temperatures. The ideal label manufacturer also understands the unique requirements of producing tamper-evident labels for the medical and pharmaceutical industries.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_6jBMAN": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Printing Options",
            "content": "<p>A good label manufacturer should have different printing options, such as thermal paper, laminations, foil stamping, and embossing, as well as a variety of adhesives. They should have custom sizing, die cutting, and coating capabilities. The more options a manufacturer has, the more likely they can come up with the perfect label for your product.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_whKcYL": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Consistency",
            "content": "<p>Your labels should be consistent in size and color from order to order. If you order labels in rolls, they should have the same thickness and tightness, as these factors affect how they dispense from automated machinery.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        },
        "collapsible_item_YVTygY": {
          "type": "collapsible_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "heading": "Customer Service",
            "content": "<p>Before getting into any business arrangement with a label manufacturer, pay close attention to how the business treats you. They should be responsive and transparent in all their dealings, taking you through the entire process to ensure you are satisfied with the end product.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "page": "",
            "open": false,
            "use_subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
